  "interpretation": {
    "headline": "Fusion substantially extends the detection horizon. At 1.0-1.5s before corridor entry fused recall is 0.696 vs camera 0.306 (2.3x); at 1.5-2.0s it is 0.545 vs 0.036. Radar alone detects essentially nothing at any lead time, consistent with its structural lateral blindness.",
    "read_recall_not_precision": "Precision and F1 are NOT comparable across bands and must not be quoted per band. Every band shares one large negative pool (thousands of non-crossing observations) while the positive count falls from ~1600 in the nearest band to a handful in the far bands, so precision is driven to near zero by construction regardless of model quality. Recall (band-specific by definition) and ROC-AUC are the interpretable columns.",
    "label_horizon_vs_realised": "Labels use a 3.0s horizon but realised entry times cluster hard at the near end: of 6,663 observations with a ground-truth entry time, the 0.0-0.5s band holds ~1,600 of the positives each configuration scores, while bands beyond 1.5s hold fewer than 20. The dataset therefore supports lead-time claims only out to about 1.5s.",
    "radar_auc_artifact": "Radar ROC-AUC appears to RISE with lead time (0.734 to 0.970) while its recall stays at 0.000. AUC is rank-based and does not require the model to cross the decision threshold; with n as low as 1-14 positives those values are unstable and must not be reported as radar improving at long range."
